IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp3-nouns`
IMPORT `cp3-deemed-contributions`
IMPORT `cp3-contributory-period`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II -- THE MINIMUM QUALIFYING PERIOD (subsections 44(2) to 44(5)).
--
-- Most benefits need base contributions "for not less than the minimum qualifying period", which the Act
-- measures differently for different benefits: a disability pension and a disabled contributor's child's
-- benefit (subsection (2): four of the last six years, or 25 years of which three are in the last six, or each
-- year since an earlier disability benefit stopped); a death benefit, a survivor's pension and an orphan's
-- benefit (subsection (3): a third of the years, at least three, or ten years); a post-retirement disability
-- benefit (subsection (4), with its own contributory period in subsection (5)). Subsections (2.1) and (2.2)
-- soften subsection (2) for a late applicant.
--
-- The facts are kept year by year (cp3-nouns.l4: `cp3 Year in a contributory period`), in order, oldest first.
-- A year is "included either wholly or partly" in the contributory period when at least one of its months is.
-- Ages go through section 2(2); subsection (3)(a) is one of the places where section 2(2) does not apply, so the
-- actual birthday is used there. Everything the section reads from another section is an input.

§ `Part II -- Division A -- the minimum qualifying period (subsections 44(2) to 44(5))`

§§ `Helpers of this module (no provision licenses them)`

-- Not a provision: the years of a record that are included wholly or partly in the contributory period (some month of the year is in it).
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
`cp3 — the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period` years MEANS
    filter (GIVEN year YIELD (year's `months of that year in the contributory period`) GREATER THAN 0) years

-- Not a provision: the last six of the years included (the record is oldest first), or all of them if there are fewer than six.
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
GIVETH A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
`cp3 — the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period` years MEANS
    reverse (take 6 (reverse (`cp3 — the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period` years)))

§§ `44(2)(a) -- the minimum qualifying period for a disability pension`

-- src:1002 | (a) a contributor is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period only if the contributor has made base contributions during the contributor’s contributory period on earnings that are not less than the contributor’s basic exemption, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2),
@ref Act s 44(2)(a) (src:1002)
GIVEN year IS A `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: base contributions were made for the year on earnings not less than the basic exemption (calculated
-- without regard to subsection 20(2): the record's `basic exemption for that year` is that figure).
-- out of range: subsection 20(2) (piece cp1): the basic exemption "calculated without regard to subsection 20(2)" is taken as a number.
`s 44(2)(a) — base contributions were made for a year on earnings not less than the basic exemption` year MEANS
    (year's `earnings on which a base contribution was made for that year`) AT LEAST (year's `basic exemption for that year`)

-- Not a provision: how many of a list of years are years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption.
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp3 — the number of years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` years MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN year YIELD `s 44(2)(a) — base contributions were made for a year on earnings not less than the basic exemption` year) years)

-- src:1003 | (i) for at least four of the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period or, where there are fewer than six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, for at least four years,
@ref Act s 44(2)(a)(i) (src:1003)
GIVEN `the number of the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period (or of all of them, where there are fewer than six) in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: the test of limb (i) on the number of years that count: at least four.
`s 44(2)(a)(i) — at least four of the last six calendar years count, by number` `the number of the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period (or of all of them, where there are fewer than six) in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` MEANS
    `the number of the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period (or of all of them, where there are fewer than six) in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` AT LEAST 4

-- src:1003 | (i) for at least four of the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period or, where there are fewer than six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, for at least four years,
@ref Act s 44(2)(a)(i) (src:1003)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: four of the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period, or, where fewer than six
-- are included, four years: in both cases at least four of the years looked at are years of contributions on earnings not less than
-- the basic exemption.
`s 44(2)(a)(i) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` years MEANS
    `s 44(2)(a)(i) — at least four of the last six calendar years count, by number` (`cp3 — the number of years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` (`cp3 — the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period` years))

-- src:1004 | (i.1) for at least 25 calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, of which at least three are in the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, or
@ref Act s 44(2)(a)(i.1) (src:1004)
GIVEN `the number of the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those years, among the last six calendar years included, in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: the test of limb (i.1) on the numbers of years that count: at least 25, of which at least three are in the last six.
`s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — at least 25 calendar years count, three of them among the last six, by number` `the number of the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` `the number of those years, among the last six calendar years included, in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` MEANS
        `the number of the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` AT LEAST 25
    AND `the number of those years, among the last six calendar years included, in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` AT LEAST 3

-- src:1004 | (i.1) for at least 25 calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, of which at least three are in the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, or
@ref Act s 44(2)(a)(i.1) (src:1004)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: at least 25 calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period, of which at least three are in the last six.
`s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least 25 calendar years, three of them in the last six` years MEANS
    `s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — at least 25 calendar years count, three of them among the last six, by number`
        (`cp3 — the number of years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` (`cp3 — the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period` years))
        (`cp3 — the number of years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` (`cp3 — the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period` years))

-- src:1005 | (ii) for each year after the month of cessation of the contributor’s previous disability benefit; and
@ref Act s 44(2)(a)(ii) (src:1005)
GIVEN `the contributor had a previous disability benefit that ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period that are the year of the cessation month or a later year` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: the test of limb (ii) on numbers: there was a previous disability benefit, and every one of the included years from the year it stopped counts.
`s 44(2)(a)(ii) — every calendar year since the previous disability benefit ceased counts, by number` `the contributor had a previous disability benefit that ceased` `the number of calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period that are the year of the cessation month or a later year` `the number of those years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` MEANS
        `the contributor had a previous disability benefit that ceased`
    AND `the number of those years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` AT LEAST `the number of calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period that are the year of the cessation month or a later year`

-- src:1005 | (ii) for each year after the month of cessation of the contributor’s previous disability benefit; and
@ref Act s 44(2)(a)(ii) (src:1005)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
      `the month of cessation of the contributor's previous disability benefit, if there was one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: for a contributor who had an earlier disability benefit that stopped, base contributions on earnings not less than the basic
-- exemption for each year after the month it stopped. A "year after the month" is read as a calendar year included in the contributory period that is
-- the year of the cessation month or a later one (NOTES.md, fork register); with no earlier benefit the limb does not apply.
`s 44(2)(a)(ii) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for each year after the month of cessation of the previous disability benefit` years `the month of cessation of the contributor's previous disability benefit, if there was one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the month of cessation of the contributor's previous disability benefit, if there was one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — every calendar year since the previous disability benefit ceased counts, by number` FALSE 0 0
    WHEN JUST ceased THEN
        `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — every calendar year since the previous disability benefit ceased counts, by number` TRUE
            (count (`the years from the year of the cessation month` ceased))
            (`cp3 — the number of years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` (`the years from the year of the cessation month` ceased))
    WHERE
        `the years from the year of the cessation month` ceased MEANS
            filter (GIVEN year YIELD (year's `calendar year of the contributory period`) AT LEAST (DATE_YEAR ceased)) (`cp3 — the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period` years)

-- src:1000 | Calculation of minimum qualifying period in case of disability pension and disabled contributor’s child’s benefit
-- src:1001 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b) and, if a disability pension is payable to a contributor, paragraph (1)(e),
-- src:1002 | (a) a contributor is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period only if the contributor has made base contributions during the contributor’s contributory period on earnings that are not less than the contributor’s basic exemption, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2),
-- src:1003 | (i) for at least four of the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period or, where there are fewer than six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, for at least four years,
-- src:1004 | (i.1) for at least 25 calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, of which at least three are in the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, or
-- src:1005 | (ii) for each year after the month of cessation of the contributor’s previous disability benefit; and
@ref Act s 44(2)(a) (src:1000-1005)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
      `the month of cessation of the contributor's previous disability benefit, if there was one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: the contributor is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period (for a disability pension
-- and, if a disability pension is payable, for a disabled contributor's child's benefit) only if one of limbs (i), (i.1) or (ii) holds.
`s 44(2)(a) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a disability pension` years `the month of cessation of the contributor's previous disability benefit, if there was one` MEANS
        `s 44(2)(a)(i) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` years
    OR  `s 44(2)(a)(i.1) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least 25 calendar years, three of them in the last six` years
    OR  `s 44(2)(a)(ii) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for each year after the month of cessation of the previous disability benefit` years `the month of cessation of the contributor's previous disability benefit, if there was one`

§§ `44(2)(b) -- the contributory period for a disability pension`

-- src:1007 | (i) commencing January 1, 1966 or when he reaches eighteen years of age, whichever is the later, and
@ref Act s 44(2)(b)(i) (src:1007)
`s 44(2)(b)(i) — the first day of 1966, the earliest start of the contributory period` MEANS YMD 1966 1 1

-- src:1011 | (iv) in relation to any benefits payable under this Act for any month after December, 1977, any month for which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year for which the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings are less than the basic exemption of the contributor for the year, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2).
-- src:1036 | (d) in relation to any benefits payable under this Act for any month after December 1977, any month for which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year for which the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings are less than the contributor’s basic exemption for the year, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2).
@ref Act s 44(2)(b)(iv), s 44(5)(d) (src:1011), (src:1036)
`s 44(2)(b)(iv) — the first day of 1978, December 1977 having passed` MEANS YMD 1978 1 1

-- src:1006 | (b) the contributory period of a contributor shall be the period
-- src:1007 | (i) commencing January 1, 1966 or when he reaches eighteen years of age, whichever is the later, and
-- src:1008 | (ii) ending with the month in which he is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph (1)(b),
-- src:1009 | but excluding
-- src:1010 | (iii) any month that was excluded from the contributor’s contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability, and
-- src:1011 | (iv) in relation to any benefits payable under this Act for any month after December, 1977, any month for which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year for which the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings are less than the basic exemption of the contributor for the year, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2).
@ref Act s 44(2)(b) (src:1006-1011)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the contributor is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph (1)(b)` IS A DATE
      `the month was excluded from the contributor's contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month for which the benefit is payable` IS A DATE
      `the contributor was a family allowance recipient for the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's basic exemption for the year of the month, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: for the minimum qualifying period of a disability pension, the contributory period starts on 1 January 1966 or when the contributor reaches
-- 18, whichever is later, and ends with the month the contributor is determined to have become disabled; it leaves out months excluded by reason
-- of disability and, for a benefit payable for a month after December 1977, months in which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year
-- whose base unadjusted pensionable earnings are less than the basic exemption.
`s 44(2)(b) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a disability pension` month `the contributor's date of birth` `the month in which the contributor is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph (1)(b)` `the month was excluded from the contributor's contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` `the month for which the benefit is payable` `the contributor was a family allowance recipient for the month` `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year of the month` `the contributor's basic exemption for the year of the month, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2)` MEANS
        `the month of a date` month AT LEAST `cp3 — the later of two dates` `s 44(2)(b)(i) — the first day of 1966, the earliest start of the contributory period` (`s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` `the contributor's date of birth` 18)
    AND `the month of a date` month AT MOST `the month of a date` `the month in which the contributor is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph (1)(b)`
    AND (NOT `the month was excluded from the contributor's contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability`)
    AND (NOT (    `the month for which the benefit is payable` AT LEAST `s 44(2)(b)(iv) — the first day of 1978, December 1977 having passed`
              AND `the contributor was a family allowance recipient for the month`
              AND `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year of the month` LESS THAN `the contributor's basic exemption for the year of the month, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2)`))

§§ `44(2.1) and 44(2.2) -- late applications for disability pensions`

-- src:1013 | (2.1) For the purpose of determining the minimum qualifying period of a contributor referred to in subparagraph (1)(b)(ii), the basic exemption for the year in which they would have been considered to have become disabled, and in which the base unadjusted pensionable earnings are less than the relevant Year’s Basic Exemption for that year, is an amount equal to that proportion of the amount of that Year’s Basic Exemption that the number of months that would not have been excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability is of 12.
@ref Act s 44(2.1) (src:1013)
GIVEN `the relevant Year's Basic Exemption for the year in which the contributor would have been considered to have become disabled` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months of that year that would not have been excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: for a contributor whose application came late (subparagraph (1)(b)(ii)), the basic exemption for the year they would have been considered
-- disabled, if the year's base unadjusted pensionable earnings are less than the Year's Basic Exemption, is the Year's Basic Exemption times the months not excluded
-- by reason of disability, over 12. Otherwise the Year's Basic Exemption stands.
-- out of range: section 20 (piece cp1): the relevant Year's Basic Exemption is taken as a number.
`s 44(2.1) — the basic exemption for the year in which a late applicant would have been considered to have become disabled` `the relevant Year's Basic Exemption for the year in which the contributor would have been considered to have become disabled` `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year` `the number of months of that year that would not have been excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` MEANS
    IF `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year` LESS THAN `the relevant Year's Basic Exemption for the year in which the contributor would have been considered to have become disabled`
    THEN `the relevant Year's Basic Exemption for the year in which the contributor would have been considered to have become disabled` TIMES (`the number of months of that year that would not have been excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` DIVIDED BY 12)
    ELSE `the relevant Year's Basic Exemption for the year in which the contributor would have been considered to have become disabled`

-- src:1015 | (2.2) A contributor referred to in subparagraph (1)(b)(ii) is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period for the purpose of subparagraph (1)(b)(i) if
-- src:1016 | (a) they became disabled in a month in which they were a family allowance recipient;
-- src:1017 | (b) in the year in which they became disabled
-- src:1018 | (i) the child in respect of which they were a family allowance recipient reached seven years of age, and
-- src:1019 | (ii) their base unadjusted pensionable earnings were less than their basic exemption, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2); and
-- src:1020 | (c) in the absence of this subsection, a disability pension would not be payable to them, but had they become disabled in the year immediately before the year in which they became disabled, a disability pension would have been payable to them under subparagraph (1)(b)(ii).
@ref Act s 44(2.2) (src:1015-1020)
GIVEN `the contributor is a contributor referred to in subparagraph (1)(b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor became disabled in a month in which they were a family allowance recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the year in which they became disabled, the child in respect of which they were a family allowance recipient reached seven years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year in which they became disabled` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's basic exemption for that year, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2)` IS A NUMBER
      `in the absence of this subsection a disability pension would not be payable to them, but had they become disabled in the year immediately before, a disability pension would have been payable to them under subparagraph (1)(b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: a late applicant who became disabled in a month in which they were a family allowance recipient, in the year the child turned seven and with
-- base unadjusted pensionable earnings below the basic exemption, is deemed to have made base contributions for the minimum qualifying period if without this
-- subsection no disability pension would be payable but one would have been had they become disabled a year earlier. The last input is a counterfactual about
-- the Act's other conditions, supplied as a fact.
-- out of range: subsection 20(2) (piece cp1): the basic exemption "calculated without regard to subsection 20(2)" is taken as a number.
`s 44(2.2) — a late applicant is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period` `the contributor is a contributor referred to in subparagraph (1)(b)(ii)` `the contributor became disabled in a month in which they were a family allowance recipient` `in the year in which they became disabled, the child in respect of which they were a family allowance recipient reached seven years of age` `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year in which they became disabled` `the contributor's basic exemption for that year, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2)` `in the absence of this subsection a disability pension would not be payable to them, but had they become disabled in the year immediately before, a disability pension would have been payable to them under subparagraph (1)(b)(ii)` MEANS
        `the contributor is a contributor referred to in subparagraph (1)(b)(ii)`
    AND `the contributor became disabled in a month in which they were a family allowance recipient`
    AND `in the year in which they became disabled, the child in respect of which they were a family allowance recipient reached seven years of age`
    AND `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year in which they became disabled` LESS THAN `the contributor's basic exemption for that year, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2)`
    AND `in the absence of this subsection a disability pension would not be payable to them, but had they become disabled in the year immediately before, a disability pension would have been payable to them under subparagraph (1)(b)(ii)`

§§ `44(3) -- the minimum qualifying period for a death benefit, a survivor's pension and an orphan's benefit`

-- src:1023 | (a) for at least one third of the total number of years included either wholly or partly within their contributory period, excluding from the calculation of that contributory period any month in a year after the year in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age and for which the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings were equal to or less than the contributor’s basic exemption for that year, but in no case for less than three years; or
@ref Act s 44(3)(a) (src:1023)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
      `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
-- Plain gloss: the years that count in the total for subsection (3): the years included wholly or partly in the contributory period, leaving out
-- (as the paragraph says) any year after the year in which the contributor reaches 65 in which the base unadjusted pensionable earnings are equal to or less
-- than the basic exemption. Reaching 65 is the actual birthday here: paragraph 44(3)(a) is one of the places where section 2(2) does not apply.
`s 44(3)(a) — the calendar years in the total, leaving out the years after 65 in which the earnings do not exceed the basic exemption` years `the contributor's date of birth` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN year YIELD NOT (    (year's `calendar year of the contributory period`) GREATER THAN `the year of the 65th birthday`
                                  AND (year's `base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year`) AT MOST (year's `basic exemption for that year`)))
           (`cp3 — the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period` years)
    WHERE
        `the year of the 65th birthday` MEANS DATE_YEAR (`s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `paragraph 44(3)(a)` `the contributor's date of birth` 65)

-- src:1023 | (a) for at least one third of the total number of years included either wholly or partly within their contributory period, excluding from the calculation of that contributory period any month in a year after the year in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age and for which the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings were equal to or less than the contributor’s basic exemption for that year, but in no case for less than three years; or
@ref Act s 44(3)(a) (src:1023)
GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: base contributions in at least a third of the years (k years of n), and in no case fewer than three years.
`s 44(3)(a) — base contributions were made for at least one third of the years, and for at least three years` k n MEANS
    (k TIMES 3) AT LEAST n AND k AT LEAST 3

-- src:1024 | (b) for at least ten years.
@ref Act s 44(3)(b) (src:1024)
GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(3)(b) — base contributions were made for at least ten years` k MEANS
    k AT LEAST 10

-- src:1022 | (3) For the purposes of paragraphs (1)(c), (d) and (f), a contributor is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period only if the contributor has made base contributions during their contributory period
-- src:1023 | (a) for at least one third of the total number of years included either wholly or partly within their contributory period, excluding from the calculation of that contributory period any month in a year after the year in which the contributor reaches 65 years of age and for which the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings were equal to or less than the contributor’s basic exemption for that year, but in no case for less than three years; or
-- src:1024 | (b) for at least ten years.
@ref Act s 44(3) (src:1022-1024)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
      `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: for a death benefit, a survivor's pension and an orphan's benefit, the deceased contributor is deemed to have made base contributions for not less
-- than the minimum qualifying period only if (a) or (b) holds. A base contribution is made for a year when section 52(3)(a) deems one made: the year's base unadjusted
-- pensionable earnings exceed the basic exemption.
`s 44(3) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a death benefit, a survivor's pension and an orphan's benefit` years `the contributor's date of birth` MEANS
        `s 44(3)(a) — base contributions were made for at least one third of the years, and for at least three years` `the number of years in which a base contribution was made` `the number of years in the total`
    OR  `s 44(3)(b) — base contributions were made for at least ten years` `the number of years in which a base contribution was made`
    WHERE
        `the years in the total` MEANS `s 44(3)(a) — the calendar years in the total, leaving out the years after 65 in which the earnings do not exceed the basic exemption` years `the contributor's date of birth`
        `the number of years in the total` MEANS count `the years in the total`
        `the number of years in which a base contribution was made` MEANS
            count (filter (GIVEN year YIELD `s 52(3)(a) — a base contribution is deemed to have been made for a year` (year's `base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year`) (year's `basic exemption for that year`)) `the years in the total`)

§§ `44(4) and 44(5) -- the minimum qualifying period for a post-retirement disability benefit`

-- src:1027 | (a) for at least four of the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period;
@ref Act s 44(4)(a) (src:1027)
GIVEN `the number of the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(4)(a) — at least four of the last six calendar years count, by number` `the number of the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` MEANS
    `the number of the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` AT LEAST 4

-- src:1027 | (a) for at least four of the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period;
@ref Act s 44(4)(a) (src:1027)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(4)(a) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` years MEANS
    `s 44(4)(a) — at least four of the last six calendar years count, by number` (`cp3 — the number of years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` (`cp3 — the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period` years))

-- src:1028 | (b) for at least 25 calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, of which at least three are in the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period; or
@ref Act s 44(4)(b) (src:1028)
GIVEN `the number of the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those years, among the last six calendar years included, in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(4)(b) — at least 25 calendar years count, three of them among the last six, by number` `the number of the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` `the number of those years, among the last six calendar years included, in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` MEANS
        `the number of the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` AT LEAST 25
    AND `the number of those years, among the last six calendar years included, in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` AT LEAST 3

-- src:1028 | (b) for at least 25 calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, of which at least three are in the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period; or
@ref Act s 44(4)(b) (src:1028)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(4)(b) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least 25 calendar years, three of them in the last six` years MEANS
    `s 44(4)(b) — at least 25 calendar years count, three of them among the last six, by number`
        (`cp3 — the number of years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` (`cp3 — the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period` years))
        (`cp3 — the number of years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` (`cp3 — the last six calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period` years))

-- src:1029 | (c) for each year after the month of cessation of the contributor’s previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit.
@ref Act s 44(4)(c) (src:1029)
GIVEN `the contributor had a previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit that ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period that are the year of the cessation month or a later year` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(4)(c) — every calendar year since the previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceased counts, by number` `the contributor had a previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit that ceased` `the number of calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period that are the year of the cessation month or a later year` `the number of those years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` MEANS
        `the contributor had a previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit that ceased`
    AND `the number of those years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` AT LEAST `the number of calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period that are the year of the cessation month or a later year`

-- src:1029 | (c) for each year after the month of cessation of the contributor’s previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit.
@ref Act s 44(4)(c) (src:1029)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
      `the month of cessation of the contributor's previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit, if there was one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44(4)(c) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for each year after the month of cessation of the previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` years `the month of cessation of the contributor's previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit, if there was one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the month of cessation of the contributor's previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit, if there was one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 44(4)(c) — every calendar year since the previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceased counts, by number` FALSE 0 0
    WHEN JUST ceased THEN
        `s 44(4)(c) — every calendar year since the previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceased counts, by number` TRUE
            (count (`the years from the year of the cessation month` ceased))
            (`cp3 — the number of years in which base contributions were made on earnings not less than the basic exemption` (`the years from the year of the cessation month` ceased))
    WHERE
        `the years from the year of the cessation month` ceased MEANS
            filter (GIVEN year YIELD (year's `calendar year of the contributory period`) AT LEAST (DATE_YEAR ceased)) (`cp3 — the calendar years included wholly or partly in the contributory period` years)

-- src:1025 | Calculation of minimum qualifying period — post-retirement disability benefit
-- src:1026 | (4) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(h) and, if a post-retirement disability benefit is payable to a contributor, paragraph (1)(e), the contributor is deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period only if the contributor has made base contributions during their contributory period on earnings that are not less than the contributor’s basic exemption, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2),
-- src:1027 | (a) for at least four of the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period;
-- src:1028 | (b) for at least 25 calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period, of which at least three are in the last six calendar years included either wholly or partly in the contributor’s contributory period; or
-- src:1029 | (c) for each year after the month of cessation of the contributor’s previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit.
@ref Act s 44(4) (src:1025-1029)
GIVEN years IS A LIST OF `cp3 Year in a contributory period`
      `the month of cessation of the contributor's previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit, if there was one` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: for a post-retirement disability benefit and, if one is payable, a disabled contributor's child's benefit, the contributor is deemed to have made
-- base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period only if (a), (b) or (c) holds.
`s 44(4) — deemed to have made base contributions for not less than the minimum qualifying period, for a post-retirement disability benefit` years `the month of cessation of the contributor's previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit, if there was one` MEANS
        `s 44(4)(a) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least four of the last six calendar years` years
    OR  `s 44(4)(b) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for at least 25 calendar years, three of them in the last six` years
    OR  `s 44(4)(c) — base contributions on earnings not less than the basic exemption for each year after the month of cessation of the previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit` years `the month of cessation of the contributor's previous disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit, if there was one`

-- src:1031 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4), the contributory period of a contributor is the period
-- src:1032 | (a) commencing when they reach 18 years of age, and
-- src:1033 | (b) ending with the month in which they are determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph (1)(h),
-- src:1034 | but excluding
-- src:1035 | (c) any month that was excluded from the contributor’s contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability, and
-- src:1036 | (d) in relation to any benefits payable under this Act for any month after December 1977, any month for which the contributor was a family allowance recipient in a year for which the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings are less than the contributor’s basic exemption for the year, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2).
@ref Act s 44(5) (src:1031-1036)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the month in which the contributor is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph (1)(h)` IS A DATE
      `the month was excluded from the contributor's contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month for which the benefit is payable` IS A DATE
      `the contributor was a family allowance recipient for the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year of the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's basic exemption for the year of the month, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: for subsection (4), the contributory period starts when the contributor reaches 18 (there is no 1966 floor here) and ends with the month the
-- contributor is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph (1)(h); it leaves out months excluded by reason of disability and, for a
-- benefit payable for a month after December 1977, family allowance months in a year whose base unadjusted pensionable earnings are less than the basic exemption.
`s 44(5) — a month is in the contributory period for the minimum qualifying period of a post-retirement disability benefit` month `the contributor's date of birth` `the month in which the contributor is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph (1)(h)` `the month was excluded from the contributor's contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability` `the month for which the benefit is payable` `the contributor was a family allowance recipient for the month` `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year of the month` `the contributor's basic exemption for the year of the month, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2)` MEANS
        `the month of a date` month AT LEAST `the month of a date` (`s 2(2) — the date a person is deemed to reach a specified age` `the contributor's date of birth` 18)
    AND `the month of a date` month AT MOST `the month of a date` `the month in which the contributor is determined to have become disabled for the purpose of paragraph (1)(h)`
    AND (NOT `the month was excluded from the contributor's contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability`)
    AND (NOT (    `the month for which the benefit is payable` AT LEAST `s 44(2)(b)(iv) — the first day of 1978, December 1977 having passed`
              AND `the contributor was a family allowance recipient for the month`
              AND `the contributor's base unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year of the month` LESS THAN `the contributor's basic exemption for the year of the month, calculated without regard to subsection 20(2)`))
